    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0681" n="667" xml:id="pg667"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Marcy to Mr. Rowcroft</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1856-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 28,
                        1856</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For reasons which have been communicated to
                    Her Majesty’s government, the President has revoked the exequatur heretofore
                    granted to you, by which you were permitted to exercise the functions and enjoy
                    the privileges of British consul at Cincinnati.</p>
                <p>I herewith send to you a copy of the act of revocation.</p>
                <p><seg type="margin">[608]</seg> *In consequence of this proceeding, the President
                    has deemed it proper that the pending prosecution against you, for the violation
                    of the neutrality law of the United States, should be discontinued.</p>
                <p>Orders to that effect have been issued to the United States attorney at
                    Cincinnati.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>W. L. MARCY.</item>
                            <item>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Rowcroft</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Her Britannic Majesty’s Consul,
                                    Cincinnati.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
